{title: A Low Whisper}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 19:9–13}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Go out and stand on the [F#]mount before the [D#m]Lord
And behold, the Lord passed [F#]by
A great and strong [C#]wind tore the moun[B]tains
But the [G#m]Lord was not in the [D#m]wind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
After the [F#]wind an earthquake
[C#]But the Lord was not [B]in the earthquake
[D#m]After the [F#]earthquake a fire
[C#]But the Lord was [B]not in the fire
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
And after the [D#m][F#]fire
The sound of a [C#]low whisper
[B]And after the [D#m][F#]fire
The sound of a [C#]low whisper [B]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D#m]What are you do[F#]ing here, [C#]Elijah [B]
{end_of_verse}
